Subject: [PATCH 04/36] bass303: sequence the 4x decimator's two halfband calls

decim_hb1(hb1, decim_hb2(hb2, os0, os1), decim_hb2(hb2, os2, os3)) ran both
calls on one filter state inside one argument list, whose evaluation order is
unspecified: gcc ran the os2/os3 pair first, clang the os0/os1 pair. On gcc the
BASS303_OS=4 build was darker (centroid -10..-13% vs Open303) and run_bass303
failed; with the calls sequenced it is 0.3-0.5%. BASS303_OS=2 (the shipped
default) compiles to identical code: no sound change on the device.
---
 firmware/src/dsp/bass303.c | 10 +++++++++-
 1 file changed, 9 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/firmware/src/dsp/bass303.c b/firmware/src/dsp/bass303.c
index 5ec78e8..1bc92cd 100644
--- a/firmware/src/dsp/bass303.c
+++ b/firmware/src/dsp/bass303.c
@@ -639,7 +639,15 @@ static void run(bass303_t *b, float *out, int n)
 #elif BASS303_OS == 2
             s = lite ? os[0] : decim_hb1(b->hb1, os[0], os[1]);
 #else
-            s = lite ? os[0] : decim_hb1(b->hb1, decim_hb2(b->hb2, os[0], os[1]), decim_hb2(b->hb2, os[2], os[3]));
+            if (lite) {
+                s = os[0];
+            } else {
+                /* two calls on one filter state: sequence them (argument evaluation order is
+                 * unspecified; gcc ran the second pair first) */
+                const float h0 = decim_hb2(b->hb2, os[0], os[1]);
+                const float h1 = decim_hb2(b->hb2, os[2], os[3]);
+                s = decim_hb1(b->hb1, h0, h1);
+            }
 #endif
 
