Subject: [PATCH 32/36] Clip keys: add the KEYS panel and the SCALE, CHORD and
 ARP pages.

The bottom strip shows the KEYS panel in clip mode. It shows the stages,
one octave with the scale, the chord name and the arp line.
A tap on SCALE, CHORD or ARP turns the stage on or off. A hold opens the
page of the stage. The keys edit the page while the button is held.
FADER BANK pins the page. < and > step the last field.
Add 13 scales and 13 chords (6th, 11th, 13th and more).
Add arp SWING, arp RHYTHM (Euclid), HUMAN velocity and chord STRUM.
The new settings use two bytes at the end of the settings.
The header shows EXT or INT for the arp clock.
Add host tests for the zones, the page logic and the new tables.
