 ### SMK-37 APC40 mkII / Loopy Pro clip launcher
 
-The SMK-37 Pro and Elite builds include an APC40 mkII-compatible MIDI identity handshake, the 40-cell APC clip-note/LED protocol, and the APC velocity color palette. Clip feedback on MIDI channels 0–15 carries the same color. The firmware trims empty outer margins but preserves internal empty cells. An 8-wide layout shows one local 8×2 view (two rows) at a time; OCTAVE− and OCTAVE+ move it down and up by two rows within the latched clip area. A layout of 3 or 4 rows and 4 or fewer columns folds onto one 8×2 view: source rows 0–1 (the lowest APC rows) map to physical pads 5–8 and 13–16, and rows 2–3 map to pads 1–4 and 9–12. The pad rows are vertically flipped while columns stay left-to-right. Holding KNOB BANK for more than 1 s toggles clip mode. In clip mode `<` / `>`, a short KNOB BANK tap and FADER BANK do nothing, and the firmware sends no APC navigation messages; change the Loopy page to reach clips outside its 8×5 APC box. The firmware stores APC feedback as it arrives (there is no staged feedback) and latches the layout 250 ms after the first burst. Seq PLAY and Seq REC send momentary APC40 Play and Record messages in clip mode, and their LEDs follow Loopy's Play and Record/overdub feedback. Configure the Loopy Record binding and overdub behavior there; Loopy Pro remains the source of clip state and color.
